# Can Prophet Forecast What Iowa Liquor Stores Will Order?

The spirits that Iowa's grocery, liquor and convenience stores (Class E licensees) bought from the state every week, 2012 to 2025: 3,370 stores, 33.3 million invoice lines. Sixty of them are forecast 13 weeks at a time, 32 times, from 2018 to 2025. Five questions:
- how much better than "the same week last year" can a store's weekly purchases be forecast, with Prophet and with a plain regression;
- whether holidays (Thanksgiving, July 4, Christmas ...) are worth a term, and how big their effect is;
- what the spring 2020 break did to the forecasts, and whether leaving it out of training helps;
- how the error depends on a store's size;
- what the raw files get wrong before any forecasting starts.

The questions follow DataCamp's "Store Sales Forecasting with Prophet" (50+ stores, holidays and promotions), answered with a walk-forward test that only ever uses the past. The page with the results and the charts is the build log:

Build log: https://mrrishit909.github.io/projects/iowa-liquor-forecast/

