# Who does data work, and does it pay?

Who calls themselves a data engineer, AI/ML engineer, data scientist or analyst in the Stack Overflow Annual Developer Survey, what they work with, how those tools go together, what they are paid once country and experience are held fixed, and where they are. Five questions:
- how many respondents hold each data role, and who answers a developers' survey as an analyst;
- which languages, databases, cloud platforms and (in 2024) libraries mark each role, against other developers;
- how the tools co-occur: the Python and SQL bundle, and which pairs travel together;
- whether the data roles are paid more, raw and like for like (same country, same years of experience, same employment type);
- where the data respondents are, and what a self-selected online survey does and does not say.

The questions follow DataCamp's "Data Science and MLOps Landscape in Industry" (roles and skills, geography), with the Stack Overflow survey as the data and static charts instead of a map. The page with the results and the charts is the build log:

Build log: https://mrrishit909.github.io/projects/dev-survey-data-roles/

